LLM text-generation architecture

1. User input
"Why was my loan application rejected?"

2. Tokenization
Text → token IDs

3. Embedding + positional information
Token IDs → numerical vectors with position information

4. Transformer layers
Attention + neural-network processing

5. Next-token prediction
Scores → probabilities → select a token

6. Repeat and decode
Append the token and predict the next one until generation stops

Final response
"Your application may have been rejected because..."


Remember: Token ID = number identifying a token; token embedding = learned vector representing it; positional information = information about its place in the sequence.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
How does next-token prediction work?

An LLM does not usually generate an entire paragraph in one step. It predicts the next token based on the tokens already available.

Suppose the current text is:
The capital of India is

The model might assign these example probabilities:

Candidate next token	Example probability
New	65%
Delhi	20%
Mumbai	10%
Chennai	5%

Step 1 The capital of India is
Step 2The capital of India is New
Step 3 The capital of India is New Delhi
Step 4 The capital of India is New Delhi .
